MENTOR: We'll work on Title, the "An easing lesson" text that's fading in at 1 s.

From 0.5 s to 1.5 s, Title moves, scales and fades at one steady speed the whole way, then stops dead at 3 s. That constant speed is called linear, and it's why the motion looks mechanical. Easing slows it down as it leaves each keyframe and as it arrives at the next.

To ease a pair, press U with Title selected so its keys show. Then select both keys of the pair and choose **Animation > Keyframe Assistant > Easy Ease** (F9). The diamond-shaped keyframes turn into hourglasses.

Ease Title's two Position moves (0.5 s to 1.5 s, and 1.5 s to 3 s), its Scale and its Opacity, and say done.

